`nix develop` drops `outputChecks` from a structured-attrs derivation again.

`develop.cc` erases `outputChecks` from the parsed `__json`, but
`StructuredAttrs::unparse` returns `verbatim`, the encoding it parsed, when
it has one. So the erase has no effect, and the dev-env derivation keeps the
checks. Measured on 2.36pre: `print-dev-env --json` of a derivation with
`outputChecks` disagreed with huggorm's port of `develop.cc`, which drops
them as 2.35 does. 2.35 has no `verbatim`.

--- a/src/nix/develop.cc
+++ b/src/nix/develop.cc
@@ -257,6 +257,9 @@
     /* Remove derivation checks. */
     if (drv.structuredAttrs) {
         drv.structuredAttrs->structuredAttrs.erase("outputChecks");
+        /* `unparse` prefers the parsed encoding, which still holds
+           `outputChecks`. */
+        drv.structuredAttrs->verbatim.reset();
     } else {
         drv.env.erase("allowedReferences");
         drv.env.erase("allowedRequisites");
